From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:37:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a mandatory pin leaves home only through the
 worker queue, and every move keeps its label [daveey]

Review 5878972889 on #1622 found two ways an old-core worker could still lease a mandatory-pin card. An old core
has no refusal() and no clear_refused_pin CAS, so it would run the card on another model.

1. Worker-first enrollment. The Board's worker-first lease checks only profile, requires and skill labels. The
   create-time attestation sees only members that are eligible now, so a held or stale old-core member could be
   assigned the card later. Now a mandatory pin never takes the worker-first route:
   - creation_decision keeps it home;
   - hub admission's pool_route refuses a denied pin when no attested queue exists, as it did while the pin
     counted as an uncarried option;
   - placement recovery never promotes or re-pins it (current_portable is False).
   The worker queue stays the one way out: there capability:mandatory-model-pin sits in runs_on, and the Board
   lease enforces it.
2. Moves. kanban_move.check() now passes the target labels through kanban_mandatory_pin.carry(), which unions the
   label into the new runs_on. This covers the agent's move, an operator move and the pickup-stall alarm's exact
   [pool:worker] move. A machine:<x> target must therefore attest it. The one exception is a pin to this machine
   (me): it runs this core. The hub-admission pickup re-place (kanban_hub_admission_pickup._fields) now carries
   the pin columns, so its queue labels keep the label too.

Non-blocking point: kanban_mandatory_pin's docstring now says "mandatory" means the model_pin_mandatory column. A
`require_model: true` body line only exempts a pin from the quota reroute, as before.

Tests (each fails on ebc69953d4, passes here):
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_mandatory_pin.py: +7 (21 total), covering worker-first exclusion, the pool_route
  refusal, no recovery promotion, the hub pickup re-place, the move to [pool:worker] and to machine:<x>
  (parametrized), and carry() for a self pin.
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_stall_repin.py: +1, the alarm's [pool:worker] move keeps the label.
RED on ebc69953d4: 8 failed. GREEN: 82/82 in those two files, and 999/999 across the 50 test files that import a
changed module.
